  "id": "Compound::DB01016 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "The integrated evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Glyburide interacts with Slc15a1, primarily through its binding to Slc15a2. Glyburide is a sulfonylurea compound that is known to inhibit the activity of the ATP-binding cassette transporter (ABC) transporter family, which includes Slc15a1 and Slc15a2. This inhibition may disrupt the transport of oligopeptides across cellular membranes, which is a key function of Slc15a2. The interaction between Glyburide and Slc15a2 is supported by multiple paths, with the lowest common ancestor linking Glyburide to Slc15a2 through the sulfonylurea class. The presence of two distinct pathways—both involving Glyburide binding to Slc15a2 and subsequent participation in transporter activity—suggests a robust and well-documented interaction. The mechanism is further supported by the involvement of Slc15a1 in oligopeptide transport, indicating that Glyburide may modulate this process. The evidence is consistent with a direct and mechanistically plausible interaction, though the exact nature of the transport disruption remains to be fully elucidated.",
